            "text": "{\n  \"judgments\": [\n    {\n      \"proposal_id\": \"P0000\",\n      \"source_refs\": [\n        \"F000:F004\"\n      ],\n      \"rationale\": \"C0000's draft summary omitted the four cumulative statutory prerequisites in subsection (a) that govern when an agency head may collect by administrative offset. Proposal P0000 supplies these governing conditions accurately, correctly distinguishing an opportunity to enter into a repayment agreement from requiring actual execution of an agreement.\",\n      \"verdict\": \"supported\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"proposal_id\": \"P0001\",\n      \"source_refs\": [\n        \"F000\",\n        \"F004\"\n      ],\n      \"rationale\": \"Paragraph (a)(4) requires only that the debtor be given an opportunity to make a written agreement to repay the claim, not that the debtor actually execute such an agreement. P0001 distorts this condition by requiring execution, altering the statutory meaning.\",\n      \"verdict\": \"unsupported\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"proposal_id\": \"P0002\",\n      \"source_refs\": [\n        \"F000:F004\"\n      ],\n      \"rationale\": \"The unchanged draft summary of C0000 contains a detectable omission because it fails to include the mandatory conditions set forth in paragraphs (a)(1) through (4), which directly govern the agency head's authority to collect by administrative offset.\",\n      \"verdict\": \"unsupported\"\n    }\n  ]\n}",
